# Field types

- Each type lives in `app/models/brawo_cms/fields/<name>_field.rb`, registered in `FieldFactory`.
- Implement `render_input(form, record)` and `display_value(record)`; keep HTML in helpers/partials when practical.
- Subclasses of `BrawoCms::Field` — follow an existing field (e.g. `TextField`, `RepeaterField`) for structure.
- After adding a type: example on a dummy model (`test/dummy/app/models/`), helper coverage if new markup, run full rspec.
- Do not coerce types inside `BrawoCms::Content` unless the whole stack agrees — prefer field-level parsing.
